status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYOSHI, SEIJI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ASAHINA HIDETAKE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>AWATA YUTAKA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HASEGAWA KAZUTOMO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOIZUMI NOBUKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIYOSHI SEIJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ASAHINA, HIDETAKE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AWATA, YUTAKA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HASEGAWA, KAZUTOMO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOIZUMI, NOBUKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYOSHI, SEIJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A digital subscriber's line transmitting method for alternately transmitting and receiving DMT symbol strings between xDSL devices through TDD-xDSL transmission, in which on the training symbol transmission side, part of the data in a DMT symbol string is redundantly added to the front, back, or both of a training symbol string during the training prior to normal communication, and the resultant symbol string is transmitted; and on the reception side, the redundant data added is deleted, and the training is carried out.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé de ligne de transmission numérique d'abonné pour transmettre et recevoir successivement des chaînes de symboles DMT entre des dispositifs xDSL par transmission TDD-xDSL. La part de données dans une chaîne de symbole DMT, côté transmission de symbole de formation, est ajoutée de manière redondante à l'avant, à l'arrière, ou aux deux, d'une chaîne de symbole de formation pendant la formation précédant la communication normale, et la chaîne de symbole résultante est transmise. Côté réception, les données redondantes sont supprimées et la formation est effectuée.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>